<article class="env-definition" id="044F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/044F">Definition <span data-tag="044F">78.18.1</span>.</a> Let $B \to S$ as in Section <a href="/tag/043A" data-tag="043A">78.3</a>. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over the base $B$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say an open subspace $W \subset U$ is <em>$R$-invariant</em> if $t(s^{-1}(W)) \subset W$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A locally closed subspace $Z \subset U$ is called <em>$R$-invariant</em> if $t^{-1}(Z) = s^{-1}(Z)$ as locally closed subspaces of $R$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A monomorphism of algebraic spaces $T \to U$ is <em>$R$-invariant</em> if $T \times _{U, t} R = R \times _{s, U} T$ as algebraic spaces over $R$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>